            <chunk name="Object" index="65">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">caa9f28b-ad35-53f5-998d-6dc089aabb95</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">ALMOND HARNESS</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">ALMOND HARNESS - machine sockets for run_gh_definition

Almond binds these params by their exact nicknames. The green INPUTS sliders and the
sample geometry to the right are DISCONNECTED in this copy: each one is replaced by the
ALMOND_IN_* param of the same value, which is what Almond writes to.

ALMOND_IN_BASE_SRF  &lt;-  Surface 'Base Srf'
ALMOND_IN_RIBS_U  &lt;-  Number Slider 'Ribs U'
ALMOND_IN_RIBS_V  &lt;-  Number Slider 'Ribs V'
ALMOND_IN_RIB_DEPTH  &lt;-  Number Slider 'Rib depth'
ALMOND_IN_BRACE_RADIUS  &lt;-  Number Slider 'Brace radius'

Outputs collect the results Almond bakes:
ALMOND_OUT_RIB_AXES  &lt;-  Iso Curve.U Isocurve (f3b2a566), Iso Curve.V Isocurve (02ed2ea4)
ALMOND_OUT_BRACE_AXES  &lt;-  Move.Geometry (cb2212fe)
ALMOND_OUT_RIBS  &lt;-  Extrude.Extrusion (63b624d5), Extrude.Extrusion (1c7ba500)
ALMOND_OUT_BRACES  &lt;-  Pipe.Pipe (9aa61bd2)

The logic is the teaching file's, unchanged. To learn the definition, open
definitions/structure-shell-roof-ribs.ghx instead.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
